From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 10:59:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Accept \??\GLOBALROOT in front of a DOS-namespace file
 name.

\??\GLOBALROOT links to the root of the object namespace, so
\??\GLOBALROOT\??\X and \??\GLOBALROOT\DosDevices\X name the same file
as \??\X. Programs build such names by putting \\?\GLOBALROOT in front of
what NtQueryVirtualMemory(MemoryMappedFilenameInformation) returns, which
on Wine is a \??\ name. get_dos_prefix_len() recognised only \??\ and
\DosDevices\, so nt_to_unix_file_name() took the name for a native object
path and the open failed with STATUS_OBJECT_NAME_NOT_FOUND.

Age of Empires II: Definitive Edition (Arxan anti-tamper) opens its own
executable and AoE2DE.dat this way to verify them. When that failed it
left its code encrypted and died on it ("Unhandled illegal instruction at
0000000142B9A04C", exit 84) before showing a window; with this it reaches
its main menu. Found by the aoe2 fork's N3 (finding N3-F1), reduced to
wine-arm64/tests/arm64-globalroot.c.

Skip any leading \??\GLOBALROOT before checking for the DOS prefixes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
index 1bfec7a..d869f9a 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
@@ -3363,14 +3363,23 @@ failed:
 static inline int get_dos_prefix_len( const UNICODE_STRING *name )
 {
     static const WCHAR dosdev_prefixW[] = {'\\','D','o','s','D','e','v','i','c','e','s','\\'};
-
-    if (name->Length >= sizeof(nt_prefixW) &&
-        !memcmp( name->Buffer, nt_prefixW, sizeof(nt_prefixW) ))
-        return ARRAY_SIZE( nt_prefixW );
-
-    if (name->Length >= sizeof(dosdev_prefixW) &&
-        !wcsnicmp( name->Buffer, dosdev_prefixW, ARRAY_SIZE( dosdev_prefixW )))
-        return ARRAY_SIZE( dosdev_prefixW );
+    static const WCHAR globalrootW[] = {'\\','?','?','\\','G','L','O','B','A','L','R','O','O','T'};
+    const WCHAR *buffer = name->Buffer;
+    unsigned int len = name->Length / sizeof(WCHAR), skip = 0;
+
+    /* \??\GLOBALROOT links to the root of the namespace, so \??\GLOBALROOT\??\X and \??\GLOBALROOT\DosDevices\X
+     * name the same file as \??\X. Programs build such names from MemoryMappedFilenameInformation. */
+    while (len - skip > ARRAY_SIZE( globalrootW ) && buffer[skip + ARRAY_SIZE( globalrootW )] == '\\' &&
+           !wcsnicmp( buffer + skip, globalrootW, ARRAY_SIZE( globalrootW )))
+        skip += ARRAY_SIZE( globalrootW );
+
+    if (len - skip >= ARRAY_SIZE( nt_prefixW ) &&
+        !memcmp( buffer + skip, nt_prefixW, sizeof(nt_prefixW) ))
+        return skip + ARRAY_SIZE( nt_prefixW );
+
+    if (len - skip >= ARRAY_SIZE( dosdev_prefixW ) &&
+        !wcsnicmp( buffer + skip, dosdev_prefixW, ARRAY_SIZE( dosdev_prefixW )))
+        return skip + ARRAY_SIZE( dosdev_prefixW );
 
     return 0;
 }
